quran[24]{c,v,t}:
  55,17,(He alone is) the Lord of the two easts and (He alone is) the Lord of the two wests.
  55,18,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,19,He is the One Who has made the two seas flow that join each other;
  55,20,There is a barrier between them; they cannot breach (their respective) limits.
  55,21,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,22,The pearls (shading green) and corals (shading red) come forth from both (the seas).
  55,23,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,24,And (under) His (control) are (also) the big vessels with lofty sails raised high (anchoring or sailing) in the sea like mountains.
  55,25,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,26,Whoever is on the earth will perish.
  55,27,"And the essence of your Lord, Who is the Master of glory and splendour and the Master of bounty and honour, will remain."
  55,28,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,29,All that are in the heavens and the earth beg from Him alone. Every moment His Glory manifests anew.
  55,30,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,31,"O both the groups (of men and jinn), soon shall We attend to your account."
  55,32,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,33,"O company of the jinn and men! If you have the power to go across the boundaries of the heaven and the earth (and overpower the universe), then go ahead. Whichever station (i.e., heavenly sphere) you will go to, there too will be His Kingdom alone."
  55,34,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,35,"The flames of pure (i.e., smokeless) fire will be sent upon both of you and (flameless) smoke (too will be sent) and you both will be unable to escape from them."
  55,36,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,37,"And when the heavens will split apart and will become rosy like burnt oil (or red leather),"
  55,38,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,39,That Day no man or jinn will be asked about his sin.
  55,40,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
